## User Stories

### Epic
> As a visitor to the UFO/UAP disclosure platform, I want curated, narrated paths through the knowledge graph so that I can understand a thesis or theme without having to know where to start.

### Story 1 — Discover and start a tour
> **As a** first-time visitor
> **I want** to see a list of guided tours with a short summary and estimated duration
> **So that** I can pick a starting point that matches my interest and time.

**Acceptance criteria**
- The Guided Tours directory lists every registered tour with cover image, title, summary, and `estimatedMinutes`.
- Selecting a tour opens the mind map with the tour active on step 1.
- If a tour was previously started, the card shows progress and a "Resume" action.

### Story 2 — Follow a tour step by step
> **As a** user taking a tour
> **I want** each step to focus the relevant entities, frame the camera on them, and explain how they connect
> **So that** I can follow the narrative without getting lost in the full graph.

**Acceptance criteria**
- Advancing a step dims unrelated nodes, highlights the step's entities, reveals edges per the step's `edgeReveal` policy, and fits the viewport to the focused nodes.
- The narration panel shows step title, markdown body, optional media/callout, and a "step N of M" indicator.
- `←`/`→` navigate steps; `Esc` exits; the panel is keyboard-operable and screen-reader friendly.
- With `prefers-reduced-motion`, camera changes are instant cuts.

### Story 3 — Drill in and resume
> **As a** curious user
> **I want** to click a focused entity to open its detail view and later return to the tour where I left off
> **So that** I can dig deeper without losing my place.

**Acceptance criteria**
- Clicking a focused node opens that entity's existing detail view/panel.
- Tour progress is persisted to `localStorage`; re-entering the tour offers "Resume at step N".
- A tour step is deep-linkable via `?tour=<id>&step=<n>`.

### Story 4 — Exit cleanly
> **As a** user
> **I want** exiting a tour to return the mind map to how it was before
> **So that** I can continue free exploration without leftover highlight or dimming state.

**Acceptance criteria**
- `exit()` restores pre-tour selection, viewport, and node/edge visibility from the snapshot.
- `tour_completed` fires on finishing the last step; `tour_abandoned` fires on early exit.

### Story 5 — Take the OOPArt tour
> **As a** user interested in anomalous artifacts
> **I want** the Out of Place Artifacts tour to walk me through representative cases and the evaluation lens used to assess them
> **So that** I understand both the claims and how the platform weighs them.

**Acceptance criteria**
- The tour presents the six steps in `out-of-place-artifacts.ts`.
- Each artifact step links at least one source `document`.
- Narration states claims as claims and names the evaluation criterion at each step.

### Story 6 — Take the Manhattan→Propulsion tour
> **As a** user interested in the secrecy/disclosure thesis
> **I want** a chronological tour from the Manhattan Project through Roswell to black physics and advanced propulsion
> **So that** I can follow the institutional pattern the platform documents.

**Acceptance criteria**
- The tour presents the seven steps in `manhattan-to-propulsion.ts` in chronological order.
- The final step explicitly separates documented record from interpretation.
- Steps reference primary-source `document` records where available; contested sourcing is flagged in narration.

### Story 7 — Author a tour without code
> **As a** content maintainer
> **I want** to define a tour as a data file and add it to the registry
> **So that** I can publish new tours without touching engine code.

**Acceptance criteria**
- Adding a `TourDefinition` to `registry.ts` makes it appear in the directory and run in the engine.
- Unresolved entity references are logged and skipped; the tour still runs.

